    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-4273",
      "problem": "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ is directed due north-east and $|\\mathbf{a}|=11.$ The vector $\\mathbf{b}$ is directed due south-east and $|\\mathbf{b}|=8.$ Find the exact value of $|\\mathbf{a}+\\textbf{b}|.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the triangle law of addition to find the sum $\\mathbf{a}+\\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14251309/assets/a122c2a1146f27a089f991f7e0bd07e4180ca4622bfc95a6b85afc83f339c11d.png)\n\nNotice that we obtain a right triangle. So, we can use Pythagorean theorem as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+\\text{b}{|}^{2} & ={|a|}^{2}+{|b|}^{2} \\\\  & ={11}^{2}+{8}^{2} \\\\  & =185\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $|\\mathbf{a}+\\textbf{b}|=\\sqrt{185}.$",
